# MAJOR GAMEPLAY UPDATE: ADVANCED MOBILITY, DASHING, GRAPPLING, AND ROCKET-POWERED FLIGHT

Implement a major movement and mobility update to the existing 2D sci-fi mech combat game.

I want the game to become MUCH FASTER-PACED, MORE DYNAMIC, AND MORE MOVEMENT-FOCUSED.

The game currently emphasizes heavy artillery, massive machines, powerful weapons, and deliberate movement. Preserve the weight and mechanical identity of the mechs, but introduce advanced mobility systems that allow players to move around the battlefield much faster.

The objective is to create a combination of heavy mechanical combat and fast-paced futuristic movement.

The player should be able to:
- Move quickly across the battlefield.
- Dash in different directions.
- Leave cinematic afterimages while dashing.
- Grapple onto buildings, structures, and environmental objects.
- Pull themselves toward objects.
- Use grappling to reposition during combat.
- Pilot an entirely new flying mech.
- Use rocket propulsion to fly.
- Fight enemies that can also fly and use rocket propulsion.

This update must integrate with the existing physics, procedural animation, weapons, AI, camera, and combat systems.

Do not remove existing mechanics or unnecessarily rewrite working systems.

