# PART 1: CAMERA SHAKE SETTINGS

Add a dedicated camera shake setting.

Some players may find the camera shake distracting, especially during fast movement, explosions, artillery bombardments, and dashing.

I want a proper setting that allows players to completely disable camera shake.

### Settings options

Add a Camera Effects section to the settings menu.

Include the following options:

**Camera Shake:**
- OFF
- LOW
- MEDIUM
- HIGH

When set to OFF, completely disable camera shake.

This must include:
- Weapon recoil shake.
- Explosion shake.
- Artillery impact shake.
- Boss ultimate shake.
- Heavy mech footsteps.
- Environmental explosions.
- Dash impact shake.
- Grappling impact shake.
- Camera shake caused by flying or landing.

When set to LOW, reduce camera movement significantly.

When set to MEDIUM, use the normal camera shake intensity.

When set to HIGH, use stronger cinematic camera feedback.

### Important implementation details

Camera shake must be handled through a centralized camera effects system.

Do not allow individual weapons, explosions, and abilities to bypass the camera shake setting.

All shake effects should respect the user's chosen setting.

Disabling camera shake must NOT disable:
- Weapon recoil physics.
- Chassis movement.
- Procedural leg reactions.
- Explosion particles.
- Screen effects.
- Visual impacts.

Only camera movement should be affected.

Also prevent excessive camera shake from overlapping when several explosions happen simultaneously.

Add a separate option for cinematic camera effects so players can reduce automatic camera zooming and dramatic camera movement during boss ultimates if necessary.

Save these preferences locally.

